From: kria-fde build <patch@local>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] efi_loader: accept unsigned images (verify outer image only)

A signed systemd-stub Unified Kernel Image (UKI) authenticates
correctly against db, but when it runs it uses the LoadImage() boot
service on the kernel embedded in its .linux section. That embedded
kernel carries no signature of its own, so efi_image_authenticate()
rejects it ("Image not authenticated" -> EFI_SECURITY_VIOLATION) and
the stub aborts with "Error loading kernel image: Security violation".

For our purposes verifying the outer, signed image is sufficient. Treat
an image that has no embedded WIN_CERTIFICATE as authenticated, so the
unsigned payload loaded by the already-verified outer image is allowed.
Signed images are still fully verified against db/dbx as before.

Applies to U-Boot v2025.01 / Xilinx xlnx_rebase_v2025.01_update
(tag xlnx_rebase_v2025.01_2025.1_update1).

Signed-off-by: kria-fde build <patch@local>
---
 lib/efi_loader/efi_image_loader.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/efi_loader/efi_image_loader.c b/lib/efi_loader/efi_image_loader.c
index 0ddf69a0918..04233ca1fba 100644
--- a/lib/efi_loader/efi_image_loader.c
+++ b/lib/efi_loader/efi_image_loader.c
@@ -605,6 +605,20 @@ static bool efi_image_authenticate(void *efi, size_t efi_size)
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * An image without an embedded signature is treated as
+	 * authenticated. Under our secure-boot policy only the outer,
+	 * signed image (e.g. a signed systemd-stub UKI) is verified
+	 * against db/dbx; an unsigned payload it subsequently loads via
+	 * LoadImage() (the embedded kernel) is accepted without an
+	 * independent signature check.
+	 */
+	if (!wincerts || !wincerts_len) {
+		log_info("Image has no signature; skipping db/dbx check\n");
+		ret = true;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * verify signature using db and dbx
 	 */
-- 
